dling your best i also won't blame  you because the fight was over faster  than you could make a coffee heck  kempachi and giriko spent more time  talking than actually fighting you  expected a big throw down that would  push kenpochi to his limits or well at  least something that lasts long despite  the majority of it happening off screen  like yummy nope kenpachi just finishes  the fight the kenpachi way a clean  bisection ending the fight in one hit  looks like our bloodthirsty friend just  got even stronger after the time skip so  much for giriko putting on all those  theatrics and blabbering about his  powers ken butchie don't give a damn is  this the shortest fight in all of bleach  or what i mean i don't have a way to  fully confirm that off the top of my  head but it's got to be somewhere there  right  fairy tale has a lot of these one-shot  fights that has become a meme but i  think that natsu vs blue note is one of  the instances where the one-hit ko feels  very satisfying  [Music]  fairy tales post timeskip avatar arc  kicks off in a big way setting the gears  off with an invasion of margaret town  courtesy of the guild orochis finn  leading the charge is an old familiar  face blue note stinger from the 10 row  island arc yes that guy who gave gildan  to run for his money is back and now our  heroes have to take care of him without  their most powerful member wendy and  sharia find themselves struggling  against his gravity magic then natsu  just comes in and we all know what  happens next he knows sales gravity  magic and absolutely dumpster's blue  note with fire dragon king's raw and  just like that invasion over and the  heroes have won i wouldn't put it any  other way post time skip blue note has  become a joke i know the fight was  written this way to make natsu look  strong but this is really pathetic for  someone who pushed gildans to the limit  back in tenro island he had all those  years to train too not good for blue  note but hilariously entertaining for  fairy tale fans  one shot fights are commonplace if  you're god suya so mahoka gave us one as  early as the first time  with all the memes floating around it  doesn't take a lot to know that mahogany  has a lot of these one-shot moments you  know scenes that just showcase how  almighty our protagonist that zuya is  compared to all the puny ants in the  mahogany universe mahuka's pretty much a  series of tatsuya flexes one after  another my favorite has got to be the  finger snap of doom versus masaki but  that battle is more of an evenly matched  and drawn out battle believe it or not  and even had dasuya suffering lethal  injuries that he didn't have the ability  to just resurrect himself so we move on  to victim number one arrogant schoolmate  hanzo taking tatsuya's weed  categorization to heart if you're so  confident in being able to win a duel  should be an easy battle against one of  those weak underdogs then right all he  has to do is to aim his cat out skill  him in magic casting and oh no that  ought to show the guy hanzo better stop  looking down on weeds because just like  any schools grading and categorizing  systems student evaluations may be the  most accurate thing in the world  demon slayer makes an appearance with  zenitsu shining moment  tinitsu is known for many things mainly  unflattering things like the noise and  the crying and the huge crush on nezuko  however while he may seem to be the most  timid and bumbling within tanjiro's  group of true companions don't let the  reputation fool you most remember the  natagumo mountain arc for the legendary  hinokami kagura and the first direct  involvement of the pillars however i'm  sure that most people would agree that  zenitsu also stole the show with his  battle against the spider demon heck if  it weren't for tanjiro's moment i think  that this would be the moment of the arc  where an unassuming zenitsu finally  unloads the power he's been hiding  inside with a one-shot victory granted  it's not against a super significant  enemy but you gotta admire zenitsu's  spirit to unleash this while suffering  from all the injuries he already had i  dare say that in this arc he's actually  the most badass of the group and that's  including the carmando siblings in the  equation there i said it  aston versus seki's up next and is this  one pretty stomp  ever noticed that a lot of these moments  so far involved one arrogant jerk  getting put in their place yeah here's  more of that this time coming from black  clover magic jewels form one of the most  fundamental trials for aspiring magic  knights so you'd expect a couple of  rotten eggs and [ __ ] somewhere in  the tournament  astar faces one such jerk in sekke who's  so confident that he can easily defeat  asta it's not hard to see why  objectively speaking zeke feels that he  has fully prepared for whatever arsenal  can throw his way with his impenetrable  shield too bad for him though his  pitiful shield is no match for arsenal  and he gets one shotted in a shocking  turn of events in hindsight the moment  feels like it can be diminished due to  sekki holding back but i don't think  that matters when we all saw this moment  it sold us on black clover and it's an  awesome one-shot knock down whichever  way you put it  next up in line is mikey's one shot on  hanma  tokyo revenges has hit the ground  running and has quickly become this  season's phenomenon blending together  the fun aspects of the time travel story  and japanese delinquents is quite the  novel premise and it does open up to a  lot of fights where both combatants dare  to go down and dirty with each other of  course fights of that nature also opened  the doors for some of the most  satisfying knockdowns and in this series  one of the more notable ones is when  mikey just flat out one shots hanma with  a kick i just love the way the moment  gets built up with all the trash talking  mikey receives then without another word  he just finishes it and follows up with  his own chilling one-liner all that  after mikey just got beaten to hell and  back it's so satisfying to see an  arrogant slob get what's coming and  hanmar gloating before getting destroyed  also doubles as one of the most  gratifying moments in the show i could  just feel the emotion in that kick talk  about making an impact am i right as we  continue with the list let's feature  everyone's favorite one-hit wonder  saitama  saitama has made a career out of  one-shotting enemies that we all know  among all of them which one is his best  though it varies from person to person  but personally i think that the second  args climax against kabuto is the best  one what i love about this scene is that  it already established what a threat  kabuto was he already beat jenos  beforehand and he still had a lot of  tricks up his sleeve then we see him  suddenly retreat from saint arma out of  instinct is that danger sense that works  so effectively when presented in visual  media intuitions are often correct and  all the more so for garbuto nope that  new form isn't going to save you and  neither is that head start you got in  roughing side armor up not when you're  up against the strongest hero of them  all one punch is all it takes your time  is up kabuto at least gobbled up an  impressive spectacle of an offensive  that would put jojo to shame no matter  how futile it ultimately ended up being  lastly we wrap this up with a one-piece  moment  knowing how big a fan i am of the series  of course we'll have a one piece moment  in here my one hit knockdown of choice  for the series is luffy versus bellamy  now let's start with a question what  kind of one shots do you like the one  where the hero just tanks or avoids all  attacks before responding with a  stomping or the one where the victim  never even gets a chance to gloat if  you're in the camp which prefers the  former then  this one's for you to be fair to bellamy  he got to show off his arsenal with  luffy not wanting to fight him he gets  free reign and the green light to start  firing himself into a supposed enemy  then he just had to make the mistake of  insulting luffy just before going for  his final attack  big mistake luffy just destroys him in  one punch just like a good hero should  do considering what happened earlier on  in the arc this is easily one of the  most satisfying moments in one piece  now that i'm done i'd like to know what  your favorite one-hit knockdowns in  anime are it could be serious or the  comedic ones just take your time to  share your thoughts in the comments  section below you could surely come up  with something that i may have  overlooked and i'd love to learn about  more moments like these if you enjoyed  this video don't forget to like the  video and share it with your friends you  can check out both memberships and my  patreon all which are linked below for  more ways to support the channel your  help would be very much appreciated i'll  be looking forward to seeing you for the  next video videotube signing off for now  and i'll see you next time  [Music]

